# localdev/.env.example  →  copy to localdev/.env and fill in. Your real .env is gitignored.
#
# Local dev authenticates with YOUR Claude subscription via the Claude Code CLI — there is NO
# Anthropic API key here. Run `claude setup-token` (headless) or `claude login` (interactive) once
# and the Agent SDK uses it. (The Anthropic workspace key is only for pushing to your Claude
# Managed Agents workspace — a separate step; see docs/building-agents.md.)
#
# The only thing you might keep here is the company MCP you were handed (URL + OAuth token), so the
# secret stays out of a committed agent.yaml. The runner expands ${VARS} in your agent.yaml from
# this file, so you can wire the MCP like:
#
#   mctools:
#     - name: company
#       url: "${MCCTX_MCP_URL}"
#
# How you actually plug the MCP into your agent is part of the job — this is just a safe place for
# the token. Never commit real secrets.

# MCCTX_MCP_URL=
# MCP_AUTH_TOKEN=
